.TH AUSCULTE 1 "2026-08-20" "realisateur" "bashified verb"
.SH NAME
ausculte \- can Zach stop looking? Composed from probes that already exist.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ausculte
.br
.B ausculte
--json
.br
.B ausculte
.I probe
.RI [ probe " ...]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Answers the one question self-dev exists to make unnecessary: is anything
broken enough that a human still has to check by hand? Every probe reuses a
tool that already exists elsewhere in this repository; this composes them
into one exit code.
.PP
THE HUMAN CHANNEL IS FIRST. Every other failure this estate has is meant to
reach Zach through zaxon, so a report where that channel itself is down and
everything else reads green is a report nobody receives.
.PP
BLIND is never folded into OK. A probe that could not look is not a probe
that passed; it is named in the report and the exit code says so.
.SH PROBES
With no arguments every probe below runs, in this order. Name one or more to
run only those.
.TP
.B channel
Can a question reach Zach at all, through the zaxon relay.
.TP
.B hosts
Does dexter serve what it declares (delegates to
.BR dexter-liveness (1)
when present).
.TP
.B arming
Are self-dev accounts armed, read from monkey's status collector.
.TP
.B propagation
Is the published verb build actually installed where it should be.
.TP
.B rot
Any answered-and-abandoned decision (delegates to
.B decision-rot.sh
when present).
.TP
.B silence
Any silenced failure path (delegates to
.BR silence-audit (1)
when present).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --json
Print one JSON object per probe instead of the aligned text report.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Every declared probe answered OK. Stop looking.
.TP
.B 5
Something declared is DOWN. The report names it.
.TP
.B 6
BLIND: at least one probe could not look, and none was DOWN. This is not
"all clear."
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dexter-liveness (1),
.BR silence-audit (1),
.BR discipline (1)
